Feature: slice-2 / firebase-hosting-deploy
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-2
Verified: 2026-05-28
Anchored to: docs/18 §3 ("Hosting & deploy")

What was built
==============
Infrastructure to deploy the marketing-site to Firebase Hosting,
without actually running a deploy in-session (no Firebase project
credentials available here).

Files touched:
- firebase.json — added a `hosting` block declaring two sites:
    • superwizor-www  → source=marketing-site (Next.js, Web
      Frameworks support)
    • superwizor-app  → public=flutter-app/superwizor/build/web
      (placeholder for Slice 5 Flutter Web target)
  Also added emulators.hosting on port 5000 for local preview.
- .github/workflows/marketing-site.yml — new GitHub Actions
  workflow. Path-filtered to fire only on marketing-site/ + proto-ts
  + firebase.json changes. Three jobs:
    1. build — pnpm install + lint + pnpm build + smoke-connect
    2. deploy-preview — fires on PRs and feat/web-app-* branches;
       deploys to ephemeral preview channel with 7-day TTL
    3. deploy-production — fires on push to main; deploys to live
       channel of superwizor-www
- marketing-site/DEPLOY.md — deploy procedure, required secrets,
  rollback flow, local-emulator preview command, DNS-cutover
  pointer to Slice 6.

Design-doc deviation (documented)
=================================
docs/18 §3 originally specified `"public": "marketing-site/out"` —
i.e. Next.js static export. Implementing that strictly would
require deleting src/proxy.ts (Next refuses static export with
middleware). We chose Firebase Hosting's Web Frameworks integration
(`"source": "marketing-site"`) which keeps the locale-routing proxy
intact and transparently deploys SSR pages to Cloud Functions in
europe-central2. Same URL surface (`/`, `/en/...`), zero code
deletion, simpler CI. The deviation + rationale is captured in
DEPLOY.md "Why `source` not `public`" section.

How verified
============
1. `firebase.json` parses as valid JSON (python3 json.load).
2. `.github/workflows/marketing-site.yml` has the expected structure
   (name, on, jobs.{build,deploy-preview,deploy-production}).
3. Final `pnpm build` after all 8 features → exit 0. Route table:
       /_not-found
       /[locale]                          → /pl, /en
       /[locale]/legal/[slug]             → 6 leaves (pl|en × terms|privacy|dpa)
       /[locale]/pricing                  → /pl/pricing, /en/pricing
   9 SSG-pre-rendered pages total + proxy middleware.
4. evidence/.../final-build.log captures the build output.
5. evidence/.../files.log lists the touched infrastructure files
   with sizes.

What's NOT in this commit (deferred)
====================================
- Actual `firebase deploy` execution — gated on having
  `superwizor-ai-25ecd` project credentials in-session. The
  workflow + config are wired; the first real deploy happens when
  a human runs `firebase deploy --only hosting:superwizor-www` or
  merges to main with the GitHub secrets populated.
- DNS cutover (superwizor.ai → Firebase Hosting) — Slice 6
  `production-dns-cutover` per PROGRESS.md.
- Terraform for the `HOSTING_DEPLOYER_SA` service account +
  Workload-Identity Federation provider — separate infra change
  outside Slice 2 scope.

